{"id":1143,"date":"2020-11-21T06:31:39","date_gmt":"2020-11-21T14:31:39","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1143"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:40:43","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:40:43","slug":"build-the-line-follower-bot","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/build-the-line-follower-bot\/","title":{"rendered":"Build the Line Follower Bot"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221631d831d\" name=\"6a221631d831d\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Body<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Bolt two short L-frames to each blueboard. The ends of the L-frames that are sticking up in the air should be facing the outer edge of the blueboard. Pay attention to their placement!<\/li>\n<li>Place the two blueboards next to each other and attach them with a 7-hole metal frame. 3 holes of the metal frame should be on each blueboard. Bolt a short standoff to the hole that&#8217;s in the middle of the two blueboards.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt a long L-frame to each blueboard next to the 7-hole metal frame.<\/li>\n<li>Just like step 2, bolt another 7-hole metal frame to the two blueboards and attach a short standoff in the middle. Make sure you use long bolts this time!<\/li>\n<li>Attach four long bolts to the inner corners of the blueboards. Pay attention to their placement! Next, flip everything over.<\/li>\n<li>Attach another blueboard using the long bolts you just attached. Flip everything back over so you see the short standoffs and the short L-frames sticking up.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1144&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1145&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1146&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221631d8473\" name=\"6a221631d8473\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Motors and battery box<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Bolt the DC motors to the short L-frames.<\/li>\n<li>Line the holes in the battery box up with the short standoffs and then bolt into place.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1147&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1148&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221631d85de\" name=\"6a221631d85de\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Wheels and Smart Inventor Board<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Attach the wheels to the motors using small black screws. The wheels will also stay attached without the screws!<\/li>\n<li>Use two long bolts to attach the Smart Inventor Board to the front of Line Follower Bot. Pay attention to the placement of the bolts!<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1149&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1150&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221631d87b4\" name=\"6a221631d87b4\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Wire the Line Follower Bot<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]To wire your Line Follower Bot, place it so the Smart Inventor Board is facing you.<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The motor on your right is M1.<\/li>\n<li>The motor on your left is M2.<\/li>\n<li>Attach the motors to their respective spots on the Smart Inventor Board (M1, M2, M3, and M4 are all marked).<\/li>\n<li>Make sure that the red wires are the in the negative position (facing the inside) and that the black wires are in the positive position (facing the outside)!<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1151&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1152&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221631d8829\" name=\"6a221631d8829\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Video<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]This video shows how the Line Follower Bot works![\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=Sv07DUEAW4U&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 6 Body [vc_column_text] Bolt two short L-frames to each blueboard. The ends of the L-frames that are sticking up in the air should be facing the outer edge&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/build-the-line-follower-bot\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1745,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":802,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1753,1777,1793,1617,423,626,1533,1438,853,144,59,171],"lesson-tag":[2163,2168,2199,2172,2171],"class_list":["post-1143","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-arduino","lesson-tag-build","lesson-tag-line-follower-bot","lesson-tag-robotics","lesson-tag-rokit-smart","module-line-follower","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1143","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":1,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1143\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":1153,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1143\/revisions\/1153"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1745"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1143"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=1143"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=1143"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}